#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# pade_approximant

#% text
# `pade_approximant(f, [x, x0, [m, k]])` gives the Pade approximant of f at x0: the rational function p/q with deg p = m and deg q = k whose series at x0 agrees with that of f to order m + k.

#% text
# `pade_approximant(f, [x, x0, n])` gives the diagonal approximant `[n/n]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The denominator is normalized to 1 at x0; x0 may be `inf` (an approximant in 1/x).

#% item
# A pole of f at x0 is taken out first: `pade_approximant(exp(x)/x, ...)` has the factor x in its denominator.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
pade_approximant(exp(x), [x, 0, [2, 3]])
#% output
#= (1 + (2/5)*x + (1/20)*x^2)/(1 - (3/5)*x + (3/20)*x^2 - (1/60)*x^3)

#% cell
pade_approximant(exp(x)/x, [x, 0, [2, 3]])
#% output
#= (1 + (1/2)*x + (1/12)*x^2)/(x*(1 - (1/2)*x + (1/12)*x^2))

#% cell
pade_approximant(cos(x), [x, 0, 2])
#% output
#= (1 - (5/12)*x^2)/(1 + (1/12)*x^2)

#% cell
pade_approximant(log(1 + 1/x), [x, inf, 2])
#% output
#= (1/(2*x^2) + x^-1)/(1 + 1/(6*x^2) + x^-1)

#% cell
series(pade_approximant(exp(x), [x, 0, [2, 3]]), x, 0, 6)
#% output
#= 1 + x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 + x^4/24 + x^5/120 + 11*x^6/7200 + O(x^7)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `series`, `apart`, `normal`
